<!--
    Systematic vocabulary extraction pass over IEC 62443-4-2 (norm-product-classification
    skill, Workflow A), first of the "high-yield norms first" batch. Every record cites its real
    source clause (queried live via find#NormClausesByDocument, not from memory) - no fabricated
    category or requirement.

    Scope of this pass: the document's own explicit 4-way component-type taxonomy (Software
    Application/Embedded Device/Host Device/Network Device, clauses 12.1/13.1/14.1/15.1) plus each
    type's component-specific technical requirements (clauses 12.2-12.3, 13.2-13.9, 14.2-14.9,
    15.2-15.13). Deliberately NOT covered in this pass (reserve, don't fabricate, per
    plm-bom-import's own "reserve don't populate" discipline): the general baseline Component
    Requirements shared by all 4 types (clauses 5-11, CR 1.1-CR 7.8, ~53 clauses, FR1-FR7
    foundational requirement families) - real, valuable vocabulary, deferred to a later pass
    rather than rushed. Also NOT available in this pass: Annex A's own device-category
    descriptions - a real gap found while doing this work, not previously known: the norm-indexer
    clause segmenter (parser/clause_segmenter.py, _EN_IEC_HEADING_RE) only matches digit-led
    hierarchical numbering ("12.1"), so lettered Annex clauses ("A.1") were silently never
    extracted into the graph at all. Flagged for a future norm-indexer fix, not addressed here.

    NCAT_IEC62443_4_2_NETDEV (Network Device) and FEAT_ZONE_BOUNDARY_MONITORING (NDR 5.2) already
    exist from the earlier single validated example (CyberNormProductClassificationDemoSeedData.xml)
    - not redefined here. This file adds the 3 sibling categories (Software Application/Embedded
    Device/Host Device) plus a second requirements group for Network Device
    (FGRP_IEC62443_4_2_NDR_REQS, linked to the existing NCAT_IEC62443_4_2_NETDEV via a second
    ProductCategoryFeatGrpAppl row - the entity's PK explicitly supports more than one group per
    category, verified against ProductDefinitionEntities.xml before relying on it).

    DeviceTypeEnumId decision: Network Device already has an exact existing match
    (moqui-device's DtNetworkDevice, parent DtPhysicalDevice) - reused, not duplicated, by
    Workflow B's classification logic (this file adds no DeviceType rows for it). For the other
    3 types (Software Application, Embedded Device, Host Device), no confident existing
    DeviceType node fits without either overloading an unrelated node or re-parenting parts of
    the existing ~150-value functional tree (e.g. Embedded Device would overlap DtController/
    DtSensor/DtSmartActuator's existing, more specific classification) - a tree reorganization
    decision out of scope for a vocabulary-extraction pass. Deliberately deferred, not forced;
    ProductCategory membership alone (which supports multiple simultaneous memberships, unlike
    the single-value deviceTypeEnumId field) already carries the classification for these 3.

    Retrofit: every ProductFeature/ProductCategory in this file now carries sourceGraphId/
    sourceGraphVertexId (extend-entity added to CyberDeviceAssetExtensions.xml), resolved to the
    real X.Y.1 "Requirement" sub-clause vertex - not the parent X.Y heading, which is an empty
    (0-length text) section title in this norm's own structure (verified: e.g. clause 13.5 "EDR
    3.10 - Support for updates" has no text, the actual "shall" statement lives in 13.5.1
    "Requirement"). Category records cite their own defining X.1 clause (12.1/13.1/14.1/15.1)
    directly, since those headings do carry real body text.
-->
